# Build context for the forecast service image (task S4 phase 3).
#
# A clean clone contains none of the heavy things below — but the OWNER'S
# working tree does, and `docker build` sends the whole directory to the daemon.
# Without this file the image would quietly carry a 35 MB dataset, 65 MB of RL
# checkpoints and eighteen 8.3 MB PatchTST runs, none of which the service
# reads. Worse, it would build fine here and fail for anyone else — the exact
# failure phase 3 exists to prevent.

.git
.venv
__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.DS_Store
.claude
.github

# Not read by the service. The dataset is the point of phase 2's design: the
# request carries its own window, so the image needs no data at all.
data
reports
sql
tests
notebooks
*.log

# Everything under models/ except the three LSTM run directories the dispatch
# chain resolves by default — the same three the .gitignore negations track.
# `models/*` excludes each entry, then the three are named back in; the
# resume checkpoints inside them are excluded again afterwards (last rule wins).
models/*
!models/load_lstm
!models/wind_lstm
!models/solar_lstm
models/*/last.pt
